# Kibana site — mounted into Caddy's conf.d ONLY by docker-compose.prod.elk.yml,
# so Kibana has a hostname only when the ELK add-on is running.
#
# Same treatment as Grafana: a real certificate, but refused unless the request
# comes from an allowlisted source address. Kibana then does its own
# authentication against Elasticsearch on top of that.
#
# The `route` block and the site-level matcher are not stylistic — Caddy sorts
# directives into its own fixed order rather than running them in file order, so
# `route` is what guarantees the address gate runs before the proxy. See the
# note in ../Caddyfile.
#
# The security_headers snippet is defined in ../Caddyfile, which imports this
# file, so it is in scope here.
{$KIBANA_HOST} {
	import security_headers

	@blocked_source {
		not remote_ip {$UI_ALLOWED_IPS}
		not path /.well-known/acme-challenge/*
	}

	route {
		respond @blocked_source "Forbidden" 403
		reverse_proxy kibana:5601
	}
}
